# --- git-crypt: private source ------------------------------------------
# This repository is public. Anything matched here is AES-encrypted in the
# repo and plaintext in the working tree for a clone holding the key.
#
# Convention: a `private/` directory at any depth is encrypted, so a project
# opts in by placing code there rather than by editing this file.
#
# For a Godot project that means game logic, core systems and shaders live in
# `godot/private/`, while vendored addons stay outside it: they are third-party
# OSS, they are public anyway, and encrypting them would hide upstream diffs.
#
# Encrypting a path is not retroactive. A file committed before it matched a
# rule keeps its plaintext in history, and `git-crypt status` will still report
# it as encrypted, because that command describes the working tree rather than
# the history. tools/hooks/pre-commit-crypt.sh is what actually enforces this.
# --- normalisation ------------------------------------------------------
# Kept above the git-crypt rules below: `binary` expands to -diff, so a later
# `*.png binary` would strip diff=git-crypt off every encrypted texture.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
pnpm-lock.yaml   linguist-generated=true -diff
Cargo.lock       linguist-generated=true -diff

# --- git-crypt rules (must stay below normalisation) ----------------------
# A later rule wins per attribute, so these come after the `binary` lines that
# would otherwise unset diff=git-crypt on encrypted images. Encryption itself
# rides on `filter` and was never affected; `git diff` on those files was.
#
# `* text=auto` above is safe here: git only normalises content it detects as
# text, and ciphertext begins with a NUL byte.
private/**              filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt
**/private/**           filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt

# .gitattributes itself must stay readable, or the filters cannot load.
.gitattributes          !filter !diff

# --- git-lfs: gilded-gazette character art -------------------------------
# Blobs live on git.kbve.com/KBVE/friendslop (see .lfsconfig); only pointers
# are in this repo. Kept below the `* text=auto` rule above and carrying -text,
# because a later rule wins per attribute and eol translation would corrupt the
# smudged binaries.
#
# These paths must never also match a git-crypt rule: git allows one filter per
# file, so an encrypted path and an LFS path are mutually exclusive.

apps/arcade/gilded-gazette/godot/assets/characters/**/*.glb   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
